<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19402" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gemmŭla</span></b> , ae, f.
		dim.
		gemma. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A little bud</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gemmulae floridae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 10, p. 253</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>the sparkling
			pupil</i> of the eye: App. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀνεχ</span>.
			8.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A small gem</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">alii autem caelo et marculo gemmulas
					exsculpunt,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Fronto Ep. ad M. Caes. 4, 3</span></i>
			 Mai.: carbunculi in ornamento auri. <i><span class="en">Vulg. Sap.
				32, 7</span></i>. 
			</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
